hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1738","**\nNarrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ad-Dawraqy, narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd ar-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurayrah (RA), who said:\n\n\I came to at-Tur (Mount Sinai)"","" where I met Ka'b al-Ahbar. I related to him some narrations from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" and he related to me from the Torah. We did not differ regarding anything until we reached the mention of the Day of Friday. I said"","" 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""In every Friday there is an hour in which"","" if a Muslim happens to pray and ask Allah for something"","" Allah will surely grant it to him.\""'\n\nKa'b said"","" 'Rather"","" it is in every year.'\n\nI said"","" 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not say that.'\n\nKa'b then went back"","" recited (the Torah)"","" and then said"","" 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) spoke the truth: it is in every Friday.'\n\nThen he mentioned the hadith at length"","" along with the story of 'Abdullah ibn Salam.\"""""""
